# Page objects

- One class per screen in `src/pages/<name>.page.ts`. Extend `BasePage`.
- Shared widgets live in `src/components/<name>.component.ts` and are constructed by the page that owns them.
- Keep locators as private fields. Keep user actions as public methods.
- Wrap each public action in `step()` from `src/utils/allure.ts`.
- Open screens with `this.goto('/relative-path')`. Do not call `page.goto` with an absolute URL.
- Do not assert inside page methods. Return text, counts, or locators the spec can assert.
- Do not import `test` or `expect` from the fixture into a page class.
- After adding a page, register it on `test` in `src/fixtures/test.fixture.ts`.

```typescript
import type { Locator, Page } from '@playwright/test';
import { step } from '../utils/allure';
import { BasePage } from './base.page';

export class HomePage extends BasePage {
  private readonly heading: Locator;

  constructor(page: Page) {
    super(page);
    this.heading = page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Example' });
  }

  async open(): Promise<void> {
    await step('Open home', async () => {
      await this.goto('/');
    });
  }

  title(): Locator {
    return this.heading;
  }
}
```
